# Client-confidential material never goes in this repo.
# Real deliverables, decks and extracted text live outside it. Anonymize before committing any example.
_client-private/
*client*.pdf
*client*.pptx

# Real-deck material stays local: raw intake machinery (extracted client text, real
# filenames, drive inventory, sealed triage) AND the pseudonymised case files, which
# carry the full text of real client deliverables. Only the labeling kit, seeded-variant
# spec and READMEs are committed.
tools/quality-reviewer/v2/eval-cases-real/intake-work/
tools/quality-reviewer/v2/eval-cases-real/real-*.md
tools/quality-reviewer/v2/eval-cases-real/real-*.gold.md

# The gold labels and capture worksheets live in the labeling/ subdir and name findings
# on real client deliverables — LOCAL ONLY, never pushed. The root rules above are anchored
# to eval-cases-real/ and do NOT reach this subdir, so it is listed explicitly.
# (Synthetic real-00.* fixtures are deliberately not matched and stay tracked.)
tools/quality-reviewer/v2/eval-cases-real/labeling/real-*.gold.md
tools/quality-reviewer/v2/eval-cases-real/labeling/real-*.worksheet.*
# The session record names client findings in prose — local only.
tools/quality-reviewer/v2/eval-cases-real/_LABELING-RECORD.md
# Secure-transfer zips of the eval set carry full client content — never commit them.
tools/quality-reviewer/v2/eval-cases-real/*.zip
# Baseline runs on the real cases: the reviewer output quotes client decks verbatim, the
# input packs are the decks themselves, and the scorecard reproduces the human gold labels.
# The whole tree is local only. The harness code (run-reviews.js, score-review.js,
# scorecard.js) and the fabricated real-00 fixtures stay tracked.
tools/quality-reviewer/v2/eval-runs/real-baseline/

# Override records embed finding text and evidence quotes from real deliverables,
# so they are client-confidential by construction (17-override-log.md section 6).
# The whole directory is ignored before the first record is written.
tools/quality-reviewer/v2/eval-runs/override-log/

# The deployable copy of the renderer, rebuilt by build-site.js. Generated, not
# authored: index.html is the source of truth. Ignored so a build that somehow
# bundled real-case reviews could not be committed from here. build-site.js
# refuses to write it at all if it carries real-case markers.
tools/quality-reviewer/v2/site/

# Heavy binaries (decks, image dumps) are kept out to keep the repo lean.
*.pptx
slides_out/
*.tmp

# Branch Awards working files carry internal branch data (budgets, metrics, client
# names in aggregate) — local only, never pushed.
branch-awards/

# Website build secrets and reference material with unclear licensing
website/.env
website/moodboard/

# Live reviewer-mockup builds render a REAL review over a REAL client deck: every quote in
# them is verbatim client material. website/ is a deployed Cloudflare Pages tree, so a live
# build committed here would publish that material to the open web. The whole directory is
# ignored rather than a filename pattern, so the rule cannot be defeated by adding a new
# file inside it. build-desk.js --live refuses to write unless its output path is ignored.
# The fabricated build (website/reviewer-mockups/index.html) stays tracked and deployable.
website/reviewer-mockups/live/

# Browser-automation artifacts: accessibility snapshots and console logs capture whatever
# was on the page. Now that a live reviewer build can render a real client deck, anything
# dropped here can contain verbatim client text. Local only.
.playwright-mcp/

# Local tooling
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.venv/

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/

# Note: small PDFs that are our own IP (evidence-base.pdf, methodology-evidence-base.pdf)
# are intentionally tracked. Client PDFs are not.

# Generated consolidated site tree (rebuilt by website/variants/tools/build-dist.mjs)
website/variants/dist/

# Cloudflare Wrangler build/deploy cache. Generated, machine-local.
.wrangler/
